# once_nothing: S4 says only that there "could have been" nothing. S5 and S6 ("if this were true", "if at one time nothing was in existence") treat it as nothing actually having existed at some time.
# necessary_exists: "necessary" in S7 means not able not to be. S8 allows such necessity to be caused by another. I read this as the same sense, with S8 asking where that necessity comes from.
